WEBVTT

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.590
I'm pretty far up now.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.530
How much do we have left?

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.520
<b>►Traverse 5% of the map (currently 4.96%)</b>

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.520
<b>►Deliver the goods to Radodorbo</b>

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.520
<b>Time remaining: approx. 15 hours, 14 minutes</b>

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.270
Oh, looking good.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:53.160
<i>The Game Master gave us two 
quests in this fourth stage.</i>

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.380
<i>"Deliver the goods to Radodorbo."</i>

00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:01.260
<i>We cleared this one when Tokitate-san and I 
brought the heads of the Deokk soldiers here.</i>

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:08.940
<i>Then we joined Shindou-san and Hakozaki-san, 
who traveled to Radodorbo in a separate group.</i>

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.070
In any case, we completed one quest.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.000
Good job!

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.690
That just leaves covering more of the map.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:18.000
We have a day and a half left.

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:19.690
Then...

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:21.010
Let's split up.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:25.670
<i>The other quest is to 
traverse 5% of the map.</i>

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:28.600
<i>To work more efficiently,</i>

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:32.220
<i>we decided to split up and 
cover ground separately.</i>

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:38.560
At this pace, we'll get it 
done with time to spare.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.530
All right!

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.850
Snow?

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:02.800
We might want to postpone our 
departure for a few days.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:07.460
The locals say they're expecting 
a nasty blizzard tonight.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:11.160
Apparently, this area has a 
somewhat unique climate.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:11.880
I see.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:15.050
I hope the heroes are all right.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:18.830
They say it gets particularly 
rough in the mountains.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.080
There you are.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.660
Kahvel-san.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:42.980
You're leaving already?

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.780
We still have a quest to finish.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.680
Then I suppose this is goodbye.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:50.920
Yeah.

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:54.450
Good work. Thanks for everything.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.790
Well, take care, Kahvel-san.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:13.810
Farewell, solitary hero.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:28.220
Captain? Captain?

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:30.910
Is something wrong?

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:33.390
Ah, no, nothing.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:35.640
We'll postpone our departure.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:38.100
It will give us a chance to 
rest before returning home.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:41.310
Makuah, you should take 
some time to relax, too.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:43.630
I will. Thank you.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:57.120
<i>"So this is to be my final stop,</i>

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:00.390
<i>where I will die before I have 
a chance to become anything?"</i>

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:03.940
<i>That's what I thought back then.</i>

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:09.310
<i>But it would seem that my battle continues.</i>

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:14.300
<i>I am a knight. 
My home is on the battlefield.</i>

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.510
<i>And that...</i>

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:20.910
<i>was just a moment's...</i>

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:27.770
<i>Great Hero, please be well.</i>

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:37.280
Oh, I can use this...

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.040
<b></b>Wizard (Creature) Gloves

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.040
<b></b>Farmer Boots

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.040
<b>Farmer Clothes (Top)</b>

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.040
<b></b>Chef Clothes (Top)

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.040
<b></b>Wizard (Creature) Clothes

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:40.570
I can choose this stuff, too?

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.420
<b></b>Farmer Boots

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.420
<b></b>Farmer Clothes (Top)

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.420
<b>Chef Clothes (Top)</b>

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.420
<b></b>Wizard (Creature) Clothes

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.420
<b></b>Chef Hat

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.960
<b></b>Farmer Clothes (Top)

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.960
<b></b>Chef Clothes (Top)

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.960
<b>Wizard (Creature) Clothes</b>

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.960
<b></b>Chef Hat

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.960
<b></b>Wizard (Creature) Accessory

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.410
It's nice that I can equip 
multiple items at once

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:49.100
as long as it's physically 
possible to layer them.

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:52.900
Good thing I changed jobs all those times.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.840
<i>Okay, this is <i>

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:01.440
<i>I thought all we had to do 
was walk around on the map!</i></i></i>

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:04.410
<i>I didn't know it was programmed 
for this to happen!</i>

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:07.490
<i>But seriously, is this for real?</i>

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:09.730
<i>Damn it. It's getting dark, too.</i>

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:12.210
<i>The temperature just keeps dropping.</i>

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:17.130
<i>Wait... could I actually 
freeze to death out here?</i>

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:21.010
<i>And if I did, would I be able to revive?</i>

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:22.370
<i>No...</i>

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:27.480
<i>Shindou-san and Hakozaki-san couldn't 
revive when the troll ate them.</i>

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:33.040
<i>So you can't revive if you're not in an 
environment where you could survive?</i>

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:35.380
<i>If I freeze to death,</i>

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:39.700
<i>and my body temperature is still 
just as low after reviving...</i>

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:44.240
I'll do some knee lifts to 
raise my body temperature.

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:50.510
Hey, this could work.

00:07:58.440 --> 00:07:59.990
This seriously sucks.

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:04.760
A sudden blizzard event isn't 
gonna make anyone happy!

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:07.040
If there's gotta be an event, 
give me some hot guys!

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:09.430
Give me a prince on a white horse!

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:13.900
<i>Just the two of us, snowed in.</i>

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:18.930
<i>We lean close together to 
warm our bodies and hearts.</i>

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:24.950
If I'm gonna die, let me die of squee!

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:29.200
S-S-Sorry!

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:35.170
Are the other three even 
able to walk in this?

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:37.450
What if they're resting?

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:39.330
<b>►Traverse 5% of the map (currently 4.98%)</b>

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:39.330
<b>►Deliver the goods to Radodorbo</b>

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:39.330
<b>Time remaining: approx. 12 hours</b>

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:39.320
For real?

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:43.570
So if I'm the only one slacking 
off, it's gonna be obvious.

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:49.910
So cold... If I stop moving, 
I'm literally gonna die!

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:53.000
Cold, cold, cold...

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.390
I wanna see Tsubasa-kyun... 
I wanna see Tsubasa-kyun...

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:58.010
I wanna see Tsubasa-kyun!

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:14.820
<i>This is killing me... I think 
my heart's about to explode...</i>

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:16.270
<i>But...</i>

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.480
I made my decision.

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:22.140
<i>When I first came to this world, I was...</i>

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:24.780
Hakozaki Kusue.

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:28.000
<b>Warrior (Sword)</b>

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:28.000
<b>Warrior (Spear)</b>

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:30.040
Warrior (Sword).

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:35.620
Yes! I got a Warrior!

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.190
I finally have someone on my side.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:45.600
I'm glad to have you here, Kusue.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:47.550
Um...

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:50.720
You might have no idea what's going on now,

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.140
but let's both do our best.

00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:55.230
I'll do whatever I can to back you up.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:58.650
S-Same to you.

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:00.950
I'm glad we're in this together.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:05.400
<i>When I first came to this world, 
I was actually kind of happy.</i>

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:11.160
<i>A lot of scary things happened, but...</i>

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:14.640
<i>I had a healthy body that let me 
be as active as everyone else,</i>

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:16.340
<i>and above all...</i>

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:19.370
We managed to beat it.

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:22.800
I'm sorry... I couldn't 
do anything to help...

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:26.290
No, it's okay.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:29.180
I'm just glad the second 
player was someone I knew.

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:31.960
Right now, that's enough for me.

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:33.540
Shindou-san?

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:37.850
Sorry... Just let me stay like 
this for a minute, okay?

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:41.480
Okay... Sure.

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:48.010
<i>I was happy that even I could 
be of use to someone.</i>

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.530
<i>Even if only a little...</i>

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.290
<i>If I could help someone else</i>

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:55.850
<i>when I never could before...</i>

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.300
<i>I won't give up.</i>

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:11.940
m 0 0 l 258 0 l 258 200 l 0 200

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:11.940
[Map]

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:11.940
►New data is added to the map starting with
the immediate 50-meter radius around the
player.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:23.590
Ugh, it's so cold...

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:30.430
<i>I've been walking almost 
nonstop since yesterday,</i>

00:11:30.430 --> 00:11:33.710
<i>and now it's snowing on top of 
that? You can't be serious!</i>

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:36.040
<i>Even if this is the fourth stage,</i>

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:38.640
<i>this quest is way too hard!</i>

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:52.210
<i>It's so quiet.</i>

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:57.730
<i>Come to think of it, I haven't been 
alone in this world for a long time.</i>

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:01.720
Huh? What does that mean?

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:05.320
<b>Defeat 1 Goblin

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:05.330
You will need to complete this que.

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:07.350
What is this place, anyway?

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:10.490
Where are the girls who were 
with me? Where are my friends?

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:14.410
The only one here is you. 
Your friends are not pres.

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:15.980
What?

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:18.330
<i>When I first came to this world,</i>

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:21.600
<i>everything I had worked to accomplish</i>

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.110
<i>was taken from me.</i>

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:28.580
<i>The ones who had always been 
on my side were my friends.</i>

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:33.730
<i>I learned that friends give you strength.</i>

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:38.250
<i>I thought as long as I was 
someone that others needed,</i>

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:41.280
<i>I wouldn't turn out like that.</i>

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:46.190
<i>That's why I worked so hard.</i>

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:53.660
<i>Only I could be responsible 
for changing my own world.</i>

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:01.640
<i>And everything I finally gained 
after all that hard work...</i>

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:10.800
<i>But in that moment...</i>

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:17.500
It sure was tough back then. I mean...

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:22.320
I don't... I don't want to 
die in this garbage world.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:25.350
No matter what.

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:27.640
So, Yotsuya-kun...

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:35.150
I need your strength in this world 
that has stripped me down to nothing.

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:38.110
Please help me.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:41.520
<i>I was really backed against a wall.</i>

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:43.040
<i>But...</i>

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:03.310
I can still keep working hard.

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:07.620
I can't die here!

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.920
<i>So heavy... My legs, my arms...</i>

00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:23.160
<i>I'm going numb...</i>

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.310
<i>But I have to keep going.</i>

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:30.130
<i>I wonder where I am... How much is left?</i>

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:34.060
<b>►Traverse 5% of the map (currently 4.991%)</b>

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:34.060
<b>►Deliver the goods to Radodorbo</b>

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:34.060
<b>Time remaining: approx. 8 hours</b>

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:38.470
Oh, good... We're all making progress...

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:41.580
Just a... little more...

00:14:56.500 --> 00:15:00.550
No... I can't...

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:03.370
I don't want... to give up...

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:05.770
No... I can't...

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:11.770
I don't want... to die... here...

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:25.930
What is this?

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:37.650
This is...

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:40.640
To hell with this!

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:46.570
Damn, damn, damn...

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:49.380
This is getting seriously bad.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:52.300
<b>►Traverse 5% of the map (currently 4.992%)</b>

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:52.300
<b>►Deliver the goods to Radodorbo</b>

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:52.300
<b>Time remaining: approx. 6 hours</b>

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:52.290
<i>No one's moved at all for a while now.</i>

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:55.830
<i>I can't blame them. 
Shindou-san and I are one thing,</i>

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:59.380
<i>but Hakozaki-san and Tokitate-san 
don't have any decent gear.</i>

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:02.690
<i>From the moment this started, 
I expected that.</i>

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:08.900
<b>►Traverse 5% of the map (currently 4.992%)</b>

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:08.900
<b>►Deliver the goods to Radodorbo</b>

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:08.900
<b>Time remaining: approx. 6 hours</b>

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:06.580
Still another nine... 
no, ten kilometers to go...

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:08.550
Ten kilometers in these conditions?

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:11.560
Can we pull it off in six hours?

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:16.940
Damn it...

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:19.920
I shouldn't have done those knee lifts!

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:24.250
<i>We're fine as long as just 
one of us survives.</i>

00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:26.640
<i>That's the rule.</i>

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:28.380
<i>But...</i>

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:33.200
<i>If I die here, my body 
temperature will drop so low</i>

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:34.610
<i>that I won't be able to revive.</i>

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:40.160
<i>This isn't the same as the other quests 
where we could revive over and over.</i>

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:47.520
<i>The damage is too much, 
both physically and mentally.</i>

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:55.150
<i>To avoid freezing to death,</i>

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:59.330
<i>it'd be best to dig out a shelter 
and wait for the storm to pass.</i>

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:03.080
<i>But if I stop moving with 
only six hours left...</i>

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:05.770
We're all dead.

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:14.480
What was that?

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:52.560
<i>A monster's attacking me right now?!</i>

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:56.040
<i>Unbelievable! This is beyond impossible!</i>

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:58.150
And running away...

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:01.310
won't work, huh?

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:33.730
Okay.

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:35.410
Bring it!

00:18:56.620 --> 00:18:58.710
That was getting pretty dicey.

00:18:58.710 --> 00:19:01.080
If this thing had been just 
a little bit stronger...

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:04.540
And attacking me in a blizzard like this?

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:07.400
It must've really been hungry.

00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:20.100
It had babies?

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:22.280
<i>Monsters are living things, too.</i>

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:25.670
<i>Am I supposed to feel bad for doing 
something so awful to them?</i>

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:32.970
If they're left alone, 
they'll either starve or freeze to death.

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:36.320
<i>But that's none of my concern.</i>

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:40.430
They're just virtual, after all.

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:57.500
Damn it!

00:19:57.810 --> 00:19:59.170
How far have I gone?

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:02.130
<b>►Traverse 5% of the map (currently 4.993%)</b>

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:02.130
<b>►Deliver the goods to Radodorbo</b>

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:02.130
<b>Time remaining: approx. 5 hours</b>

00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:01.440
<i>Five hours left...</i>

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:10.370
<i>There's one thing I've 
made up my mind about...</i>

00:20:11.050 --> 00:20:15.980
So... I want to help everyone 
now, while I'm healthy...

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:16.980
That's why I...

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:22.360
<i>And it's where I stand 
compared to everyone else.</i>

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:24.710
Please help me.

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:30.990
<i>I consider all life to 
be not equal, but fair.</i>

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:34.170
<i>If there's anyone worth more than me,</i>

00:20:34.570 --> 00:20:36.580
<i>or anyone stronger than me...</i>

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:38.760
I won't let them die.

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:47.610
<i>If we can't clear this quest, 
we'll all die in the real world.</i>

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:50.920
<i>Why us? Why here?</i>

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:53.880
<i>Why are we being forced to do all this?</i>

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:56.570
<i>If I don't even know that yet...</i>

00:20:56.800 --> 00:20:58.760
Like hell I'm gonna die!

00:21:01.350 --> 00:21:02.920
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:07.980
<i>If I die right now...</i>

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:12.740
<i>We're all...</i>

